Lineage of the RDNA4 (gfx1201) enablement
-----------------------------------------
The gfx1201 kernel enablement this port descends from was first cracked by
Rob Smith (`tcclaviger`) for the vLLM 0.18.1 line and distributed as the image
`tcclaviger/vllm-rocm-mxfp4-nvfp4`: the working RDNA4 base (gfx1201 hipBLASLt
plus MXFP4/NVFP4 MoE kernels). That work was published as source at the time and
forward-ported by this project to vLLM 0.19.1 in
`Capicua25x/vllm-rocm-rdna4-legacy` (archived), and from there to the 0.26.1
branch carried here. Without his work none of this exists. His RDNA4 work is
distributed as Docker images under `tcclaviger`. This notice exists so the
lineage remains on the record.

Separately, `vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp4/rdna_fp8.py` takes its
design lineage from Rob's `_matmul_fp8_ogs` (0.24 line, W8A8): the same
per-K-group scale fold on WMMA v2. The MXFP4 nibble→e4m3 unpack, the three-regime
dispatch (fused decode / weight-only mid-M / dequant+hipBLASLt prefill) and the
integration are this project's work.

Original in this port (not derived from the above)
--------------------------------------------------
  * RdnaMxfp4Fp8LinearKernel -- the FP8-WMMA decode path (rc6), whose scale-fold
    design follows Rob's `_matmul_fp8_ogs` as noted above.
  * A gate relaxation on upstream's 3D split-KV path so small-q spec-decode verify
    shapes can use it (MAX_QLEN_3D, token-count capacity check) -- 11 lines on a
    kernel by Burkhard Ringlein, Jan van Lunteren, Chih-Chieh Yang and Thomas
    Parnell. Arrived at independently; equivalent relaxations were proposed upstream
    first in vllm-project/vllm #44652, #45450 and #46724, none merged as of 2026-08.
  * The RDNA4 gating in mxfp4_utils.py and compressed_tensors_moe_w4a4_mxfp4.py.
  * Model bring-up, serving recipes, and the A/B validation campaigns.

Forward-ported, not original -- derived from the lineage above:
  * RdnaMxfp4LinearKernel (weight-only MXFP4), the RDNA4 branch in _swizzle_mxfp4,
    and the MXFP4 MoE routing: forward-ported from this project's 0.19.1 patch set,
    itself derived from Rob Smith's tcclaviger/vllm-rocm-mxfp4-nvfp4 RDNA4 work.
  * The RDNA4 triton_kernels graft the MXFP4 path depends on (RDNAMXValueLayout /
    mxfp4_dequant_rdna, and the RDNA branches in _matmul_ogs.py, opt_flags.py,
    target_info.py): same lineage. It is NOT in upstream triton_kernels. This
    source repository does not carry it, but the published Docker image does --
    see below.

Original to this project but carried OUTSIDE this branch, and so not part of the
source in this repository:
  * The fp8-KV attention overlay for ROCm (fp8 query input so K/V are not
    dequantized inside the KV loop) - applied at container build time.
  * A clean-room Triton head-dim-512 flash-prefill chunking implementation whose
    blueprint comes from llama.cpp (MIT); no llama.cpp code was copied. It belongs
    to the 0.19.1 line.

